      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was platted in 1857, but its post office has been operating since 1855, predating the official platting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofgenevamn.com/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Milton Morey became Geneva’s first recorded settler in 1855, building a log cabin near Geneva Lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/geneva_minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The arrival of the railroad in the late 19th century sparked local creameries and grain handling, boosting the economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/geneva_minnesota",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "European immigrants settled in Geneva during the mid‑19th century, drawn by fertile southern Minnesota lands amid post‑Civil War expansion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/geneva_minnesota",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Geneva’s early development was aided by its position along key transportation routes, a typical advantage for 19th‑century Midwestern towns.",
